# Thesis: Professor Feedback (Current Status)

Reference: advisor meeting summary. Use this for design choices and evaluation plans.

## Durable Advisor Constraints

### Reward framing
- Keep evaluation centered on reward maximization under deadline, not only goal reachability.
- Include intermediate reward behavior in analysis when relevant.

### Heuristic interpretation
- Separate time-to-goal estimation from probability-of-success estimation; conservatism in time does not imply conservatism in success probability.
- If sampling is used to support admissibility claims, distinguish between many samples at one node and one sample across many nodes.

### Planning graph usage
- Treat root-graph reuse with caution: it can be optimistic because deeper nodes commit to only one realized action path.
- Helpful actions should bias exploration, not restrict the action set.

### Value propagation
- Temporal constraints can break naive value propagation assumptions.
- Arguments about convergence/optimality should clearly state optimism assumptions in both estimates and propagation.
